meta { name: 1 Availability (ownership-guarded), type: http, seq: 1 }
get { url: {{calendarUrl}}/api/v1/calendar/availability/{{providerEmail}} }
tests {
  test("200 for the owner, 403 for anyone else", function () {
    expect([200, 403, 404]).to.include(res.getStatus());
  });
}
docs {
  **This route was IDOR-able before F-016.** It called `RequireAuthorization()` but never `OwnershipGuard`,
  so any registered user could read any provider's 30-day availability. Every sibling service already
  guarded; Calendar was the one family that did not — and nothing caught it, because no test in the
  solution executed a route table.

  Change `{{providerEmail}}` to a provider you are not, and you now get `403`.
}
